    "content" : "In that case, the boundary of each face in G is a cycle. Assume that c is the smallest number of vertices that need to be removed from G to make it C k -free, and let v 1 ,v 2 ,...,v c be one such set of vertices. Then c ≤ k , since we can remove vertices of a k -cycle to make it C k -free. Moreover, for any i,j ∈ [ c ], there exists a k -cycle in G such that v i is contained in the k -cycle, but v j not."
